From a3f82900533ccb40077a96dbee629836d5ac1c5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:39:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: Drop the delayed capture buffers with the
 others

A decoded buffer that the firmware still holds as a reference (read
only) waits on inst->delayed_process until the firmware lets go of it.
When all capture buffers go back to userspace (stream off, an error),
it stayed on that list, and delayed_process_buf_func queued it to the
firmware again once both queues streamed again, while the client queued
it itself too. Android's seek (streamoff and streamon of both queues)
did that on msm8996: the firmware failed (Err_Fatal in
video_decoder_utils.c), and the work then removed the buffer from the
m2m queue a second time (v4l2_m2m_buf_remove_by_buf on LIST_POISON, an
oops).

Empty the list when the capture buffers are returned. A seek then
decodes on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
index 6b773ee42..4023a243c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/helpers.c
@@ -2032,6 +2032,15 @@ void venus_helper_buffers_done(struct venus_inst *inst, unsigned int type,
 		while ((buf = v4l2_m2m_src_buf_remove(inst->m2m_ctx)))
 			v4l2_m2m_buf_done(buf, state);
 	} else if (type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE) {
+		struct venus_buffer *vbuf, *n;
+
+		/*
+		 * Buffers waiting for the firmware to let go of them go back
+		 * too: else delayed_process_buf_func queues them again later,
+		 * after a restart of the stream, or removes them twice
+		 */
+		list_for_each_entry_safe(vbuf, n, &inst->delayed_process, ref_list)
+			list_del_init(&vbuf->ref_list);
 		while ((buf = v4l2_m2m_dst_buf_remove(inst->m2m_ctx)))
 			v4l2_m2m_buf_done(buf, state);
 	}
